ledger: optional write-ahead log directory for the blockstore

If the environment variable COFDP_SOLANA_WAL_DIR is set and not empty, the
blockstore keeps the write-ahead log (WAL) of its RocksDB in that directory
instead of in the RocksDB directory (<ledger>/rocksdb). With PiDir-Binding the
directory can be a P-Directory of its own, so that the WAL is written with its
own PID. Unset or empty: upstream behaviour.

Every process that opens the blockstore (solana-genesis, solana-validator,
solana-ledger-tool) reads the variable; give them all the same value. RocksDB
creates the directory if its parent exists, and does not create a new
blockstore while the directory holds WAL files of another one, so the
directory must be empty when the ledger is created.

Base: solana-labs/solana tag v1.18.26
      (commit d9f20e951a06b61e4505da0955228020b96a8915)
Apply: git apply 0003-ledger-optional-blockstore-wal-directory.patch
